Modifications
-------------

1. server/channels/app/limits.go — AGPL v3.0

   scripts/patch-user-limits.sh rewrites the constants maxUsersLimit and
   maxUsersHardLimit, which upstream v11.3.3 sets to 200 and 250, to the value
   of the MM_MAX_USERS build argument. The server binary is then rebuilt from
   the patched source and replaces the one shipped in the base image.

   This path is not in the Apache-2.0 carve-out, so this modification is the
   one that makes the running server a modified AGPL work and triggers the
   section 13 obligation.

   The rebuilt binary is compiled without the `enterprise` and `sourceavailable`
   build tags and with BuildEnterpriseReady=false, so no source-available
   enterprise code from server/enterprise/ is compiled into it.

2. server/i18n/*.json — Apache License 2.0

   scripts/patch-i18n-email-subjects.sh prefixes every translation whose id
   matches api.templates.*subject, and api.admin.test_email.subject, with
   "mattermost::reject ". Outbound SMTP is configured with a subject rule that
   drops messages carrying that prefix.

3. webapp client assets — Apache License 2.0

   scripts/patch-root-html.sh injects a stylesheet link into client/root.html,
   and static/overrides.css overrides theme variables and hides announcement
   bars.

Modifications 2 and 3 fall under the Apache-2.0 carve-out rather than the
AGPL. They are listed here because Apache-2.0 section 4(b) asks that modified
files carry prominent notice of the change, and because they are part of the
Corresponding Source for the running service either way.


Original work
-------------

Everything else in this directory — the Dockerfile, the scripts under
